  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes (175 tests, 0 failed), including the new store and API tests.\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- `reserve`, `confirm`, `release` and `getAvailable` follow the spec.\n- Time comes only from the store's `clock`, and a reservation counts as expired when `clock() >= creation + ttlMs`.\n- `removeItem` now checks against available stock instead of physical stock, so reserved units can't be removed.\n- `confirm` also returns `{ sku, stock }`, which the API uses for its 200 response.\n- Reservation ids are `res-1`, `res-2`, and so on.\n- An expired reservation stays stored until it is released, so confirming it keeps returning `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` rather than `RESERVATION_NOT_FOUND`.\n- `ttlMs` isn't validated, since the spec didn't ask for it.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`.\n- `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the statuses you specified.\n- `POST /reservations` returns 409 for `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` and 400 for anything else, including `INVALID_QTY`.\n\nThe new tests are appended to `test/store.test.js` and `test/api.test.js`.",
